# Hero Section Enhancements Plan

Add dynamic, interactive elements to the Hero section to improve engagement and visual appeal.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component] [Hero](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/proyecto%20inf_1/src/components/hero)

#### [MODIFY] [HeroTitle.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/proyecto%20inf_1/src/components/hero/components/HeroTitle.tsx)
- Implement a `TextCycler` logic to rotate between different security and developer-focused phrases.
- Add fade transitions between phrases using CSS classes.

#### [MODIFY] [AnimatedBackground.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/proyecto%20inf_1/src/components/hero/components/AnimatedBackground.tsx)
- Add a scroll listener to track `window.scrollY`.
- Pass scroll progress as a CSS variable or directly as styles to the background elements (orbs) to create a parallax/scroll-reactive effect.

#### [MODIFY] [AnimatedBackground.module.css](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/proyecto%20inf_1/src/components/hero/components/AnimatedBackground.module.css)
- Use CSS variables for `transform` properties to react to the scroll position efficiently.
- Add subtle scale and blur changes based on scroll depth.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- Scroll the page to ensure the background orbs move/react smoothly.
- Observe the Hero sub-heading to verify it cycles through phrases with proper transitions.
- Check for performance issues during scrolling.
